>> title: Restaurant Style Dal Khichdi
>> servings: 6
>> prep time: 30 minutes
>> cook time: 30 minutes
>> course: main
>> cuisine: Indian

= Rice =

Rinse @basmati rice{1%cup} thoroughly with water. Soak for ~{10-15%minutes}.

Add the soaked rice and @salt{} to taste to boiling water in a #pot{} and cook for ~{10-15%minutes}. Strain the cooked rice and set aside.

= Dal =

Wash @toor dal{1%cup}, @chana dal{1/4%cup} and @masoor dal{1/4%cup} thoroughly. Soak for ~{30%minutes}, then drain.

Heat @ghee{1%tsp} in a #pressure cooker{}. Add @cumin seeds (jeera){1%tsp} and let them splutter. Add @ginger{1%inch}(julienned), the soaked and drained dal, @water{5%cups}, @turmeric{1%tsp} and @salt{} to taste.

Stir and pressure cook on medium flame for 3-4 whistles. Switch off the flame and let the cooker depressurize naturally before opening the lid. Give it a nice stir.

= Masala =

Heat @ghee{1%tbsp} in a #wok{}. Add @cumin seeds (jeera){1%tsp} and let them splutter.

Add @onion{2}(medium, chopped) and cook until translucent, about ~{5%minutes}.

Add @whole red chillies{2-3}, @garlic{2%tbsp}(chopped), @green chillies{3-4}(chopped) and @ginger{1%inch}(chopped). Sauté for ~{1%minute}.

Add @tomatoes{2}(medium, chopped), @salt{} to taste, @turmeric powder{1%tsp}, @coriander powder{1%tbsp}, @red chilli powder{1%tsp}, @amchur powder{1%tsp}, @garam masala{1%tsp} and @kasuri methi{1%tsp}. Cook until the tomatoes are mushy.

= Combine =

Add the cooked dal and mix well.

Add the cooked rice, mix well and cook for ~{3-4%minutes}.

Add water to adjust the consistency and cook for another ~{4-5%minutes}.

= Smoke =

Place a @live charcoal{1} in a small bowl set on the khichdi and pour a few drops of @ghee{}. Cover and smoke for ~{3-4%minutes}.

= Finish =

Remove the charcoal. Add @kasuri methi{1%tsp} and @lemon juice{1%tsp} and give it a nice stir. Garnish with @fresh coriander leaves{1%tbsp}(chopped).

= Tadka =

Heat @ghee{1%tbsp} in a #pan{}. Add @cumin seeds (jeera){1%tsp}, @red chilli powder{1%tsp}, @asafoetida (hing){1/2%tsp}, @whole red chillies{2-3} and @fried onions{3%tbsp}. Mix, then pour over the hot khichdi and serve.
